#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""aria-dl: downloader for people and for AI agents.

Torrents, magnet links, HTTP(S) (aria2c), and video sites (yt-dlp). Humans get a one-line status. Agents get one JSON value on stdout, documented exit codes, and `aria-dl tools` for function calling.

Usage:
  aria-dl add SOURCE [SOURCE ...] [--file FILE] [--dir DIR] [--when now|night] [--name LABEL] [--limit RATE] [--retries N] [--cookies-from-browser BROWSER[:PROFILE]] [--proxy URL] [--no-proxy] [--media] [--audio] [--max-height N] [--json]
  aria-dl list [--json]
  aria-dl status ID [ID ...] [--wait] [--timeout SEC] [--json]
  aria-dl pause ID [ID ...] | all [--json]
  aria-dl resume ID [ID ...] | all | failed | paused [--json]
  aria-dl remove ID [ID ...] | failed | complete [--json]
  aria-dl log ID [-n N] [--json]
  aria-dl tick                                   (LaunchAgent safety net, on job exit, and at the next retry)
  aria-dl cookies refresh [--browser auto|chrome|brave|edge|firefox|safari|vivaldi[:PROFILE]] [--json]
  aria-dl cookies status [--json]
  aria-dl config get [KEY] [--json] | config set KEY VALUE [--json] | config unset KEY [--json]
  aria-dl version [--json]
  aria-dl schema                                 (output shapes and exit codes, JSON)
  aria-dl tools [--json]                         (function-calling tool definitions, JSON)

Global flags work before the command or after it: --json, --yes / --non-interactive, --version.
ARIA_DL_JSON=1 forces JSON. ARIA_DL_YES=1 is the same as --yes. A non-TTY stdin is never prompted.
--json prints one pretty JSON value on stdout (not JSON Lines). Progress and human errors go to stderr. jq is optional.

Multiple tasks:
  - Pass several SOURCE arguments at once
  - Or pass --file urls.txt (-f - for stdin), one source per line (# comments and blank lines ignored)
  - Or pipe lines into stdin: pbpaste | aria-dl add --when night

--when now   : start immediately, any network (default)
--when night : only 22:00-08:00 and only when the default route is Wi-Fi; pauses outside that
Concurrency  : up to 2 media (yt-dlp) + 3 aria2c jobs run at once; extras queue and auto-start as slots free.
Retries      : yt-dlp is started with --retries 5 --fragment-retries 5 --retry-sleep exp=1:30.
               A non-zero exit (except aria2c code 7, which stays "waiting") is retried
               --retries N times (default 5, env ARIA_DL_MAX_RETRIES, 0 disables) in state
               "retrying", with backoff 2m, 5m, 15m, 30m, then 60m. One sleeper runs tick
               at the next retry time. resume of a failed or retrying job resets the counter.
Bulk         : resume failed re-queues failed and retrying jobs. resume paused re-queues
               paused jobs. resume all is paused, failed, waiting, and retrying.
               remove failed / remove complete forget those job records only.
               Selectors can be mixed with IDs and are deduplicated. Text mode prints
               "resumed N jobs (...)" ; nothing matched prints "no jobs matched".
Cookies      : --cookies-from-browser BROWSER[:PROFILE], else ARIA_DL_COOKIES_FROM_BROWSER,
               else cookies_from_browser in ~/.local/share/aria-dl/config.json, else the
               Netscape file cookies/youtube.txt. Never both --cookies and --cookies-from-browser.
               On macOS, background jobs cannot read browser profiles. Run
               `aria-dl cookies refresh` once in Terminal to copy YouTube/Google cookies
               into that file (mode 0600). auto picks the first logged-in browser.
Proxy        : optional yt-dlp --proxy for media jobs only. Never changes the system proxy.
               youtube_proxy applies to YouTube; proxy applies to every media job.
               Precedence: --proxy/--no-proxy on the job, then ARIA_DL_YOUTUBE_PROXY /
               ARIA_DL_PROXY, then config.json. "" or "none" disables. If the proxy
               port is closed, that attempt goes direct.
Jobs live in ~/.local/share/aria-dl/jobs/<ID>/ ; downloads resume automatically (--continue).
Same URL is the same job id (no duplicate). Re-adding a finished or running job reports that id and leaves it.

Exit codes:
  0 success (status without --wait is success whenever the id exists)
  1 failed (bad source, partial batch, or --wait ended failed)
  2 usage error
  3 no unique job for that id
  4 --wait ended with YouTube bot-check or a network error
  5 aria2c or yt-dlp is missing (job is kept; resume after install)
  6 --wait timed out
  130 interrupted
JSON never includes cookie values or proxy usernames/passwords. Proxy fields are host:port.
`aria-dl schema` and AGENTS.md describe the fields. See README "Use with AI agents".
"""
